// `t[i]$~ v` on a variable of its own, «N» times over «N» elements. Writing one
// element in place does not depend on how many there are, so the whole is
// linear; an engine that copies the collection to write it is quadratic.
t = []
@ i:1..«N» { t$+ 0 }
@ k:1..«N» { t[(k % «N») + 1]$~ k }
>> t[1] + t$# ¶
